<title>
Definetly worth it!
</title>
<date>
November 3, 2006
</date>
<reviewer>
Jane E. Kennedy "Mom of 3 under 4yrs"
</reviewer>
<reviewer_location>
Strasburg VA
</reviewer_location>
<review_text>
This is the first juicer I have ever used or bought. I found it very easy to use & clean (as long as you do it right away!!!) Do Not let the pulp dry on the screen! It seems very sturdy & it is fun. My family has made a lot of juice since buying this product & I have found so many uses for the pulp. The vegetable juice is hard to find, the right mix & looks a little weird but once you get the hang of it gazpacho & vegetable juices are delicious (refrigerate vegetables firt) & the pulp left over is great as a filler for meatloaf or hamburgers or pasta sauce. Fruit juices are easy & delicious (try a lime w/ tropical fruit, yummy), The product states you can juice small apples whole, they do have to be very small but cutting them in half or quarters isn't hard & that way you can extract the seeds & use the pulp as applesauce for little ones. Bananas cause a mess & you don't really get juice but we used them with other fruits & mixed the pulp back in with the juice for wonderful smoothies! You do get a lot of juice from this machine & my only complaint is you still have to use a lot of fruit for enough juice for more than 1 or 2 people (we have 5 in our family) so it does get expensive but we love this machine. Perfect for a first time juicer or someone who has been juicing for a while. I do have one more secret, to juice leafy things like spinach, ball it up first & if you're using it with something like tomatoes cut the core out of the tomatoe & stuff a ball of spinach inside. You'll get a lot more juice from the greens that way. Also be careful with onions & garlic, you will get loads of fresh onion juice!! It gave me an actual buzz! Worth the money especially if you compare it to other expensive machines or read the reveiws of similar priced ones. I don't normally right reveiws or rave about anything but this product was worth my time
</review_text>
</review>
