<title>
Kids and Math, Kids and Cooking
</title>
<date>
October 28, 2000
</date>
<reviewer>
Mary T. Skinker
</reviewer>
<reviewer_location>
Irvine, CA, USA
</reviewer_location>
<review_text>
You're cooking with your 11-year-old, who's pretty skilled at math, but conversions are beyond what's been taught, at least in practical application.  The Amco measuring equivalent chart allows you to keep those elusive math solutions at eye-level.  It creates a great opportunity to &quot;cook and learn&quot;...get the job done, and while you're both chewing on those wonderful cookies that great kid just created, you can teach the math that relates to what just happened. If you want your child, as I do, to know why math and science will always be important in their lives, this little magnetic tool on the refrigerator will give you the chance prove your point!  Go for it
</review_text>
</review>
