<title>
classy mission style furniture
</title>
<date>
September 8, 2004
</date>
<reviewer>
Shelley Shay
</reviewer>
<reviewer_location>
Denton, TX **(God Bless the USA!!
</reviewer_location>
<review_text>
I have 4 of these in my home and I love them. The shelves are adjustable and the unit is easy to assemble. The instructions are pictures only and the pictures so closely match the subtle differences in each piece, the only way you will mess up assembly is if you try to do it without referring to the schematic. Using the proper tools and not over-tightening the screws, the shelves should theoretically last forever as long as you are only loading books & not bricks in the shelves. I accent my shelves with knick-knacks along with the books. The simple style is beautiful without being boring and the color is rich. If you can't afford custom and/or raw furniture, this is the next best thing - and it doesn't look like cheesy laminate stuff like those O'Sullivan kits
</review_text>
</review>
