</date>
<reviewer>
S. Yax "long-time crockpot user"
</reviewer>
<reviewer_location>
Fairview, TN
</reviewer_location>
<review_text>
I'm actually online today searching for a NEW slow-cooker.  This one, which I've owned for about 9 months now, DOES NOT COOK SLOWLY! The tender, fall-apart kind of results you expect to get from meat cooked in a crockpot are NOT what you get with this thing.  It's convenient to clean, store, & re-heat; but roasts turn out rubbery, vegetables don't get done, & soups don't do any better than they'd do in a pot on the stove.  And that's basically all this thing is: a pot on a heating element... with a cord of all of 2 feet!  This is NOT a slow-cooker.  Don't bother with it
</review_text>
