<review_text>
I just moved from a suburban house to a high-rise condo, and the one thing I thought I'd miss was grilled food. OK, so this isn't quite the same as Webber-ing in the backyard, but it's surprisingly close. I have grilled steaks, hamburger, shishkabobs, and hotdogs on this thing, all with excellent results: quick, thorough cooking time, nice &quot;grill lines&quot; on the meat, and most importantly for me, no smoke (there was some steam from partially-thawed hamburger patties, but that's it). As for cleaning, I've found it easy and convenient: the grill, tray and base separate and the nonstick surface of the grill unit is actually nonstick. I highly recommend this grill
</review_text>
</review>
