Celia Lemonik "celial"
</reviewer>
<reviewer_location>
Great Neck, NY United States
</reviewer_location>
<review_text>
After peeling the coating off innumerable nonstick pans and warping even a legendary Magnalite skillet with excessive heat and use, I came home to cast iron. It is indestructable, formidable, utterly forgiving cookware. A dutch oven and a  skillet reside permanently on the stove top and always do a superior job of cooking whatever is tossed in them. Chili, soups and stews come out full of character. The kids are always &quot;frying up&quot; sausages, eggs, pancakes. Cleanup is a breeze, and the seasoning of the pans becomes a labor of love. My other pots basically just sit in the cupboard
</review_text>
</review>
