<review_text>
This is a heavy-duty, commercial constructed bakeware! Muffins are well baked in this pan. Good heat conducting & easy release. However, the muffins are truly "mini". Each muffin cup measures 1-3/4 inches in top diameter, 1-1/4 inches in bottom diameter, and 3/4 inch deep, which is too small for me to use with the mini muffin paper lining cups I have. (I also have a Farberware 12-cup mini muffin pan, which fits the paper lining fine.) I just have to wash 24 cups every time after I use it, which bothers me a little! I've never put any nonstick bakeware/cookware in the dishwasher even though it's dishwasher safe. WearEver did carry lifetime warranty, but you have to pay for the shipping to send the item back to them before they send you the replacement one
