<title>
It's Just a Honing Steel
</title>
<date>
December 2, 2001
</date>
<reviewer>

</reviewer>
<reviewer_location>

</reviewer_location>
<review_text>
Make sure to read what Amazon's editorial reviewer says.  Most people think that &quot;sharpening&quot; steels sharpen.  They don't.  They hone or straighten the edge.  For a dull blade, you need a good diamond-impregnated steel.  After I got one of the latter, I hardly ever use the Henckels steel.  Henckels knives have a pretty hard edge which, in my experience, tends to dull more than bending.  The Henckels honing steel will sharpen the knife, but only slightly, and the ridges in the steel will quickly wear out if you use it for this purpose
</review_text>
</review>
<review>
<unique_id>
