<review_text>
I just got done putting my new KitchenAid short turner through its paces and I am very impressed with its performance.  Although this tool is smaller than its big brother in the KitchenAid lineup, it's actually a normal sized spatula/turner compared to most other brands.  It is right at home in 9&quot; - 11&quot; skillets and handles omelette turning extremely well.  It is flexible enough not to tear and damage delicate foods such as omelettes, yet sturdy enough to detach burnt on hash browns from a cast iron skillet.  Like the other silicone tools made by KitchenAid, it cleans up beautifully in the dishwasher (no leftover egg residue!).  I would highly recommend this product
</review_text>
